    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a `timezone` field to the Owner response, derived from the locality/region via the fixed table (NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney, VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne, QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane).\n\nTo keep structural impact low, I put the logic in its own small, cohesive unit rather than growing any existing class:\n\n- **New `OwnerTimezone` helper** (`rest/advice/OwnerTimezone.java`) \u2014 a single static `of(owner)` method (CC\u22482, WMC_other=0) that reads the region prefix from the owner's `customerCode` and looks it up in the pinned region\u2192IANA map, returning `null` for regions not in the table. Mirrors the existing `OwnerTelephoneDisplay`/`OwnerMembershipLevel` helper pattern.\n- **One `@Mapping` line** in `OwnerMapper` (an annotation-only interface with no method bodies, so essentially zero surrounding complexity to hold).\n- **One `timezone` schema entry** in `openapi.yml`, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\nThe acceptance test (`$.timezone` = `Australia/Sydney` for a Sydney/NSW owner) and the rest of the suite pass.",
